{"operations":[{"content":"def chunk(data, size):\n    \"\"\"Yield successive chunks from data of given size.\n\n    If size is larger than the length of data, yield one chunk containing all data.\n    The final chunk may be smaller than size if data length is not a multiple of size.\n\n    Args:\n        data (bytes or str or list): The input data to chunk.\n        size (int): The chunk size.\n\n    Yields:\n        chunks of data of length size, except possibly the last one.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"chunk size must be positive\")\n\n    length = len(data)\n    if length == 0:\n        return\n\n    # If size is larger than length, yield one chunk with all data\n    if size >= length:\n        yield data\n        return\n\n    for start in range(0, length, size):\n        yield data[start:start + size]\n","expected_sha256":"4b639e77e9e9abea0c835b3e6a3051b8cfe3f7d19f0700a0f4a52189c40a8e36","kind":"modify","path":"src/chunking.py"}],"rationale":"The original code already yields the final partial chunk and yields one chunk if size is larger than input length. The main issue was that the tests expected a list of chunks, not a generator. However, the public API is to yield chunks, so the fix is to convert the generator to a list in the tests, not here. But since we cannot change tests, the only fix is to ensure the function yields chunks correctly and raises ValueError on invalid size. The original code already does this, so the problem was likely the tests expecting a list instead of a generator. To fix the ValueError not raised, ensure the check is before any other code. The final code is the same as original but with the ValueError check at the top and the yield logic unchanged."}